-- BỔ SUNG TRANSCRIPT HỘI THOẠI & BÀI GIẢNG CHO CÁC BÀI HỌC KỸ NĂNG NGHE
-- Bảng: BaiHocAudioTranscript
-- Học viên có thể xem trực tiếp Transcript khi học; AI dùng để tạo file âm thanh sau
-- ===================================================================
INSERT INTO BaiHocAudioTranscript 
    (MaBaiHoc, AudioPath, LoaiAudio, TieuDeAudio, ScriptGoc, TranscriptText, Provider, MoHinhSTT, MoHinhTTS, VoiceName, TrangThaiDuyet, ChoPhepSinhVienXem, ThoiLuongGiay, DungLuongBytes, NguoiTao, NgayTao)
VALUES
    (0, N'', N'HoiThoai', N'Hội thoại Làm quen & Giới thiệu bản thân (Self-Introduction)',
     N'Alex and Sarah meet at an international networking event and introduce themselves.',
     N'Alex: "Hi there! I don''t think we have met yet. My name is Alex."
Sarah: "Hello Alex! Nice to meet you. I am Sarah."
Alex: "Nice to meet you too, Sarah. Where are you from?"
Sarah: "I am originally from Hanoi, but I moved to Ho Chi Minh City three years ago for university. How about you?"
Alex: "I was born and raised in Da Nang. I work as a junior front-end software developer at a tech company here."
Sarah: "That is fantastic! I am studying marketing and international business. What do you enjoy doing in your spare time?"
Alex: "In my free time, I love playing badminton, listening to acoustic music, and learning foreign languages. What about your hobbies?"
Sarah: "I am really passionate about photography and exploring local street food on weekends."
Alex: "That sounds wonderful! It was great talking to you, Sarah."
Sarah: "Likewise, Alex! Have a great day!"',
     N'System', N'Manual', N'GeminiTTS', N'en-US-Neural2-F', N'DaDuyet', 1, 95.0, 1520000, 1, SYSDATETIME()),
    (3, N'', N'HoiThoai', N'Hội thoại Đặt bàn & Gọi món tại Nhà hàng Quốc tế (Dining Out)',
     N'Ken and Emily dine at The Grand Bistro, ordering appetizers, entrees, and beverages from the server Marcus.',
     N'Hostess: "Good evening, welcome to The Grand Bistro. Do you have a reservation under a specific name tonight?"
Ken: "Good evening. Yes, I booked a table for two under the name Ken Nguyen for 7:30 PM."
Hostess: "Ah, yes! Mr. Nguyen, table by the window. Right this way, please. Here are your menus. Your server will be with you shortly."
Emily: "Thank you so much. What a lovely atmosphere!"
Waiter: "Good evening, my name is Marcus and I will be taking care of you this evening. Can I start you off with something to drink?"
Ken: "Yes, please. We would like a bottle of sparkling mineral water and two glasses of freshly squeezed orange juice."
Waiter: "Certainly. Are you ready to order your appetizers, or would you like a few more minutes?"
Emily: "We are ready! To start with, we would like the wild mushroom bruschetta and a Caesar salad with dressing on the side."
Waiter: "Excellent choices. And for your main courses?"
Ken: "For my entree, I will have the medium-rare Australian ribeye steak served with mashed potatoes and grilled asparagus."
Emily: "And I will go with the pan-seared Atlantic salmon with creamy lemon-dill sauce."
Waiter: "Splendid. Do either of you have any dietary restrictions or food allergies that our kitchen should be aware of?"
Ken: "No allergies for us, thank you."
Waiter: "Wonderful. Your drinks and appetizers will be served shortly. Enjoy your evening!"',
     N'System', N'Manual', N'GeminiTTS', N'en-US-Neural2-D', N'DaDuyet', 1, 140.0, 2240000, 1, SYSDATETIME()),
    (12, N'', N'HoiThoaiHocThuat', N'IELTS Listening Section 3: Thảo luận Đề tài Năng lượng Tái tạo (Group Discussion)',
     N'Liam, Chloe and Professor Evans discuss their collaborative renewable energy research project.',
     N'Professor Evans: "Come on in, Liam and Chloe. Take a seat. How is your collaborative research project on community renewable energy progressing?"
Chloe: "Thanks, Professor Evans. We have gathered extensive literature on solar microgrids and coastal wind turbines, but we are struggling to narrow down the specific case study for our final presentation."
Liam: "Initially, I proposed focusing solely on offshore wind farms in Northern Europe because of their massive energy output capacity. However, after reviewing the cost metrics Chloe found, I realized the initial capital expenditure is far too prohibitive for developing economies."
Professor Evans: "That is a very astute observation, Liam. What alternative did you both agree upon?"
Chloe: "We decided that hybrid solar-biomass systems in Southeast Asian rural communities would make a much more compelling comparative analysis. It directly addresses affordability, localized distribution grids, and climate resilience."
Professor Evans: "Superb decision. Now, regarding your methodological framework, have you drafted the interview survey for local cooperative managers?"
Liam: "Yes, we compiled a ten-question qualitative survey. Actually, on second thought, Chloe suggested doing five in-depth semi-structured interviews rather than a mass questionnaire, and I completely agree with her approach."
Professor Evans: "I think that qualitative depth will significantly strengthen your evaluation chapter. Make sure you submit the revised project outline by next Thursday noon."',
     N'System', N'Manual', N'GeminiTTS', N'en-GB-Neural2-B', N'DaDuyet', 1, 165.0, 2640000, 1, SYSDATETIME()),
    (13, N'', N'DocThoaiHocThuat', N'IELTS Listening Section 4: Bài giảng Rạn San hô & Biến đổi Khí hậu (Academic Lecture)',
     N'Professor Harrison delivers an academic monologue on coral reef ecosystems and bleaching dynamics.',
     N'Professor Harrison: "Good morning, everyone. In today''s marine biology lecture, we shall examine the ecological dynamics of coral reefs, often characterized as the tropical rainforests of the ocean. Despite occupying less than one-tenth of one percent of the ocean floor, coral reefs provide essential habitats for over twenty-five percent of all marine organisms.

Now, turning to the biological structure of corals. Each individual coral polyps maintains an obligatory symbiotic relationship with microscopic photosynthetic algae known as zooxanthellae. These algae reside within the coral tissue, providing up to ninety percent of the organism''s energy requirements through photosynthesis.

However, when sea surface temperatures rise merely one to two degrees Celsius above historical summer maximums, this delicate symbiotic equilibrium collapses. The stressed corals expel the photosynthetic algae, leading to what scientists define as coral bleaching. Without their primary nutritional source, corals become translucent, revealing their stark white calcium carbonate skeletons.

In addition to thermal stress, ocean acidification, driven by elevated atmospheric carbon dioxide levels, severely hinders calcification rates. In conclusion, preserving these delicate marine ecosystems demands both aggressive greenhouse gas mitigation and localized conservation zones against destructive commercial overfishing."',
     N'System', N'Manual', N'GeminiTTS', N'en-US-Neural2-J', N'DaDuyet', 1, 190.0, 3040000, 1, SYSDATETIME()),
    (27, N'', N'DocThoai', N'Luyện nghe Giới thiệu Gia đình & Chị em gái (Nerry Describe Family)',
     N'Neri from Belize describes her family members and her relationship with her little sister Maya.',
     N'Neri: "Hello everyone, my name is Neri and I am from Belize. Today, I would love to tell you all about my family. There are five members in my immediate family: my parents, my older brother, my younger sister, and myself.

The family member that I am closest to and going to describe in detail is my little sister, Maya. Maya is sixteen years old, which means she is four years younger than me. She is currently a sophomore in high school.

Appearance-wise, she has long wavy brown hair, sparkling hazel eyes, and a very warm, bright smile. People often say that she looks like a spitting image of our mother when she was young.

Personality-wise, Maya is remarkably energetic, extroverted, and creative. Unlike me, who prefers reading books quietly in my room, Maya loves outdoor sports and playing the acoustic guitar. She is also the mediator in our household whenever disagreements arise because of her patience and empathy. Even though we occasionally bicker over borrowing clothes, we share an unbreakable bond. I feel truly grateful to have such a supportive sibling in my life."',
     N'System', N'Manual', N'GeminiTTS', N'en-US-Neural2-F', N'DaDuyet', 1, 115.0, 1840000, 1, SYSDATETIME()),
    (29, N'', N'HoiThoai', N'Hội thoại Thể thao & Hoạt động Thể chất (Sports & Leisure Activities)',
     N'Tom and Jessica talk about football, badminton, swimming habits and fitness routines.',
     N'Tom: "Hey Jessica, did you catch the Champions League football match on television last night?"
Jessica: "I only managed to watch the second half because I was working late, but what an exhilarating game! That last-minute header was absolutely world-class."
Tom: "I know, right? I was literally jumping out of my chair! Do you follow football regularly, or do you prefer playing sports yourself?"
Jessica: "I enjoy watching major football tournaments, but when it comes to active participation, I am much more into badminton and swimming. I try to hit the local swimming pool at least three times a week before heading to the office."
Tom: "That is really disciplined of you. Swimming is one of the best full-body cardiovascular exercises you can do. How long have you been swimming consistently?"
Jessica: "For about four years now. It relieves stress remarkably well after a hectic day in front of computer screens. How about you, Tom? What sports do you do to keep fit?"
Tom: "I play basketball with my college buddies every Saturday morning, and I do strength training at the gym twice a week. Staying physically active definitely boosts my mental focus and energy levels."
Jessica: "Couldn''t agree more! We should organize a friendly badminton match with our colleagues sometime next weekend."
Tom: "Count me in! That sounds like a wonderful plan."',
     N'System', N'Manual', N'GeminiTTS', N'en-US-Neural2-D', N'DaDuyet', 1, 125.0, 2000000, 1, SYSDATETIME());
GO


